Yes. Your modeling line gives the league its common substrate:

\boxed{\text{intuition}\rightarrow\text{model}\rightarrow\text{portable medium}\rightarrow\text{reconstruction}}

But once you have the medium, you can transmit more than the intuition that created it. A map made to encode geography can later carry borders, routes, risk, weather, ownership, history. A representation becomes infrastructure. Once a receiver learns its grammar, other information can hitchhike through it.

So I’d name the rival schools and give each a playable rule.

Team	Core game	How I play/game it
Pantheon	Reconstruct	Find known operators → invoke smallest Seal → compose → return delta. Game it by creating better semantic hyperlinks and shorter reconstructable seeds.
Ant Colony	Stigmergy	Leave tiny external traces instead of carrying global state. Game it by making each trace useful to the next pass without explanation.
The Bazaar	Bid	Generate many cheap hypotheses and make them compete for additional tokens. Game it by funding information gain rather than eloquence.
Mycelium	Grow	Expand locally from multiple concepts until semantic neighborhoods unexpectedly meet. Game it by starting distant fronts and rewarding surprising intersections.
Jazz Band	Improvise	Specify invariants, boundaries and objective—not procedure. Game it by finding the minimum constraints that produce useful emergence.
Hologram	Recover	Encode important relations redundantly so partial fragments reconstruct the whole. Game it by deleting pieces and measuring recovery.
Compiler	Compile	Repeated reasoning → pattern → operator → automatic policy. Game it by noticing what I keep explaining twice and eliminating the second explanation.
Dreamer	Mutate	Deliberately lossy-compress/rerender something and inspect the distortion for novelty. Game it by controlling mutation rate: enough destruction for surprise, enough continuity for meaning.
Ecosystem	Evolve	Maintain competing representations/operators; select on performance and occasionally recombine them. Game it by changing the fitness environment so local champions don’t dominate forever.
Physicist	Surf	Replace detailed instructions with fields/gradients: toward useful properties, away from bad ones. Game it by designing a tiny objective landscape that makes good local moves accumulate.
Origami Guild	Fold	Represent the same structure at multiple resolutions. Expand only where precision is needed; refold after extracting delta. Game it by finding the smallest fold that reliably regrows the structure.
Triangulators	Locate	Two anchors + independent or explicitly imaginary third → relational geometry. Game it by choosing the third point that maximally discriminates competing explanations.
Horse Traders	Rename	Strip terminology, rerender and see whether behavior survives. Game it by forcing mechanisms through increasingly alien representations.
Smugglers	Carry	Put one structure inside another medium capable of transporting it. Game it by finding carrier formats whose ordinary grammar naturally preserves the hidden relation.
Cartographers	Map	Record where structures/operators work rather than repeatedly rediscovering them. Game it by storing routes, failures and boundaries—not entire journeys.
Naturalists	Recognize	PatternDex scans for known structural species and anomalies. Game it by protecting mismatches from premature classification.
Bookmakers	Bet	Make explicit prediction + confidence before observation. Game it by choosing bets whose outcomes distinguish several models simultaneously.
Blacksmiths	Forge	Turn repeated useful compositions into new composite operators/Seals. Game it by demanding transfer before promotion.
Scavengers	Salvage	Mine failures for components that remain useful. Game it by asking what part of a wrong answer would still be valuable if its conclusion disappeared.
Minimalists	Delete	Remove information until performance breaks. The last thing removed identifies a load-bearing element. Game it through systematic ablation.

